  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>A metal is a material that, when freshly prepared, polished, or fractured, shows a lustrous appearance, and conducts electricity and heat relatively well. Metals are typically malleable (they can be hammered into thin sheets) or ductile (can be drawn into wires)</p><p>On moving top to bottom of the periodic table metallic character increases and on moving left to right metallic character decreases.</p><p>Metallic character is directly&nbsp;proportional to the atomic size.</p><p>The correct order of atomic size of the given elements is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>Mg</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>Be</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>Si</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>.</p><p>Hence, correct order of metallic character is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>Mg</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>Be</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>Si</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math></p><p>All these elements are form 3rd period except beryllium which is from second period</p><p>Na&nbsp;is an alkali metal</p><p>Mg and Be&nbsp;are&nbsp;alkaline earth metals,&nbsp;</p><p>Phosphorous belongs to a group which is commonly called as pnicogens.</p><p>Si belongs to 14th group</p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
